Subject: [PATCH] volumetric fog: remove the unused shadow_sampler declaration and binding

The last remaining bind-group failure was a comparison sampler bound into a slot
the layout declared as filtering:

  bgl:VolumetricFogProcessShaderRD:9:set0   binding 22
    supplied  sampler  compare="greater"
    expected  sampler  type="filtering"   visibility=ShaderStage::None

Nothing in that chain was inferred wrongly, which is why it needed a different
kind of fix from 0021, 0029 and 0032. WebGPU binding 22 is Godot binding 11
doubled by the combined-sampler split, and volumetric_fog_process.glsl declares:

  layout(set = 0, binding = 11) uniform sampler shadow_sampler;

That declaration is the only occurrence of shadow_sampler in the entire file.
Every real shadow read builds its sampled image from linear_sampler instead:

  texture(sampler2D(directional_shadow_atlas, linear_sampler), ...)
  texture(sampler2D(shadow_atlas, linear_sampler), ...)

So the reflection was right: ShaderStage::None is not a defect in the use
analyser, it is the correct answer for a resource that is declared and never
referenced. Tint had no compare-sampling to infer from and emitted a plain
sampler; the driver correctly derived "filtering" from that; and fog.cpp
nevertheless inserts the renderer's comparison-enabled sampler at binding 11, in
both the process and copy uniform sets. Visibility zero does not disable
bind-group resource validation -- the entry still exists and the supplied
resource still has to match its declared type.

The resource is dead, so the fix is to remove it rather than to describe it more
accurately. Removing the declaration and its matching uniform block eliminates
the entry entirely, which is the only outcome that does not leave the layout
claiming behaviour the shader never performs.

Bindings are explicitly numbered, so removing 11 leaves a hole rather than
renumbering 12-21; WebGPU binding 22 simply ceases to exist.

Deliberately NOT done:
  * marking the entry Comparison -- validates the bound object while keeping a
    resource in the shader interface that has no semantic role
  * substituting a dummy filtering sampler -- 0014's adaptation machinery could
    silence this, but it would conceal dead state instead of removing it
  * generically dropping every visibility-None entry -- too broad for one dead
    binding, and 0014 exists partly because an earlier textual use analysis
    wrongly marked genuinely used helper-function resources invisible. That rule
    could resurrect exactly that class of failure.

The renderer's comparison sampler itself is untouched. Forward+ scene shaders,
Forward Mobile and render_forward_clustered all create and use one legitimately;
only volumetric fog's dead copy is removed.

Unlike 0032, this is NOT a backport: current Godot master still carries the
unused declaration. It is a clean candidate for an upstream pull request, and the
evidence is unusually strong -- the shader's real shadow reads use
linear_sampler, reflection reports no stage visibility, the bound object has an
incompatible comparison type, and removal can have no effect on shader output
because the resource is statically unreachable.

diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/environment/volumetric_fog_process.glsl b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/environment/volumetric_fog_process.glsl
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/environment/volumetric_fog_process.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/environment/volumetric_fog_process.glsl
@@ -74,7 +74,6 @@
 layout(rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 10) uniform restrict writeonly image3D dest_map;
 #endif
 
-layout(set = 0, binding = 11) uniform sampler shadow_sampler;
 
 #define MAX_VOXEL_GI_INSTANCES 8
 
diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/fog.cpp b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/fog.cpp
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/fog.cpp
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/fog.cpp
@@ -910,15 +910,6 @@
 
 		{
 			RD::Uniform u;
-			u.uniform_type = RD::UNIFORM_TYPE_SAMPLER;
-			u.binding = 11;
-			u.append_id(p_settings.shadow_sampler);
-			uniforms.push_back(u);
-			copy_uniforms.push_back(u);
-		}
-
-		{
-			RD::Uniform u;
 			u.uniform_type = RD::UNIFORM_TYPE_UNIFORM_BUFFER;
 			u.binding = 12;
 			u.append_id(p_settings.voxel_gi_buffer);
